ef 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050104 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186051045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1031 "Unit Tangent Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1033 1794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1034 0.828049307226423 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050685 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "5ee1f34c-598f-5608-8eb7-1e1ffa254cd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186166467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186166468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186166469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186166470 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186166471 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166466 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6706dd19-f83f-5a69-b331-b8b66eafd0da" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166467 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1, 2, 1⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166467 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166467 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cedcb2ec-f9cf-5b2d-97d1-73c92e6a4657" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166468 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2, 1, 0⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166468 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166468 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d5dc64fb-366a-50d0-b0de-982441d7d6c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166469 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨ - 1,-1,-1⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166469 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166469 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dd03ee71-8291-5f27-8e14-186f1aff231e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166470 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}⟨ - 1, 1, 2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166470 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166470 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd08544a-892b-5d85-961b-7deb4532cf5a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166471 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨ - 1,-1, 2⟩" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166471 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166471 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b18103a-c14d-523c-b469-c099662d1c5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166677 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8595" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166677 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,t,4⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,4,-t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166677 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6a54cb2-ea48-57b1-bf2d-7aac09915159" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166677 #edb/ref 1074 "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,t,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,4,-t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & t & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ 4 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & t \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}⟨(-{t}^{2}-16),-(0-0),(0-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}⟨-({t}^{2}+16),0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166678 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8596" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166678 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at the point $t=\\pi$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3,4⟩, \\\\ N(\\pi ) & =⟨1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166678 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b2a775f5-4a27-5cba-931f-2a45db305152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166678 #edb/ref 1074 "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(\\pi ) & =T(\\pi )\\times N(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3,4⟩\\times ⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨(0-0),-(0-4),(0-(-3))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166679 #edb/ref 1069 "e-8597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166679 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166679 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e805dcee-247b-5aa3-9856-f7bd48bd1a78" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166679 #edb/ref 1074 "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $\\mathbf N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf N(t)= \\dfrac{\\mathbf T'(t)}{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $\\mathbf{N}(t).$ To do this, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡4t+16{sin}^{2}⁡4t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16({cos}^{2}⁡4t+{sin}^{2}⁡4t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩}{(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\times ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-0,-(-{sin}^{2}⁡4t-{cos}^{2}⁡4t),0-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,1,\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048616 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167496 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186262808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387810 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395658 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166835 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "6ef73a00-12f7-5818-85a9-d8b5e2582bfe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167543 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362368 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186371714 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186371728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating a Specific Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166836 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "91ea3125-c2b7-56d0-97d8-4e54b2c01524" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186167544 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186362381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373435 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186387817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186166679 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166837 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "93d895a2-73eb-5141-b56d-48090debf57b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186167731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1045 "Binormal Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186167731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186166979 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "bda11fb3-0944-54f5-924b-435fbfe6a4d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167498 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186360346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167498 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167498 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167498 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167498 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "553afed7-053a-5b06-8cb8-cd7b8f67d1b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167498 #edb/ref 1074 "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩}{(\\frac{1}{3})}=⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨({sin}^{2}⁡t-(-{cos}^{2}⁡t)),-(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-0),(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167543 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186166466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167543 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99414" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167543 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t = 0$, given that\n\n$T(0)|= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1, 1, 1⟩,; N(0)|= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨ - 1, 1, 0⟩$.\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167543 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38d9f4a8-a08e-535a-9477-a86a4bf7e353" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167676 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167676 #edb/ref 1061 31928 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167676 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a6b5756d-4634-5ea9-aec5-a8beb78d3e41" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167676 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166835 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167677 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167678 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167677 #edb/ref 1061 31929 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167677 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "171b5dbe-8666-5a5c-8f90-fe3b44d099a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167677 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167678 #edb/ref 1061 31930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167678 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "45a7a61e-103e-532f-aa53-42180b78442d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167678 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186166837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167731 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186167676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167731 #edb/ref 1061 34413 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167731 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ec2925b5-6f20-57e1-ac41-26fc9b56da32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186167731 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186168115 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168115 #edb/ref 1064 "The **binormal vector** to a curve $C$ defined by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{B}(t) = \\mathbf{T}(t) \\times \\mathbf{N}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{T}$ and $\\mathbf{N}$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal vectors, respectively.\n\nThe diagram below shows the binormal vector to a curve at some point $P$ on the curve. \n\nTo demonstrate, consider the curve\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\left\\langle 2\\sin t, \\: 2\\cos t, \\: t \\right\\rangle.\n\\]\n\nAt [math]t=\\dfrac{5\\pi}6,[/math] the point on the curve, unit tangent, and principal normal are, respectively, given by\n\n\\begin{align*}\n\\mathbf{r}\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) &= \\left\\langle 1, -\\sqrt3, \\dfrac{5\\pi}{6} \\right\\rangle, \\\\[5pt]\n\n\\mathbf{T}\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) &= \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt5}\\left\\langle -\\sqrt3, -1, 1 \\right\\rangle, \\\\[5pt]\n\n\\mathbf{N}\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) &= \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left\\langle -1, \\sqrt3, 0 \\right\\rangle.\n\\end{align*}\n\nUsing the formula to calculate the binormal vector, we have\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align}\n\\mathbf{B}\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\right)\t&= \\mathbf{T}\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) \\times \\mathbf{N}\\left(\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}\\right) \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt5}\\left\\langle -\\sqrt3, -1, 1 \\right\\rangle \\times \\dfrac{1}{2}\\left\\langle -1, \\sqrt3, 0 \\right\\rangle \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt5}\\, \\begin{array}{|ccc|}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\mathbf i & \\mathbf j & \\mathbf k \\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-\\sqrt3 & -1 & 1 \\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-1 & \\sqrt3 & 0\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\end{array} \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt5}\\left[ \\ \\begin{array}{|cc|}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-1 & 1 \\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\sqrt3 & 0\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\end{array} \\,\\mathbf i -\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\begin{array}{|cc|}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-\\sqrt3 & 1 \\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-1 & 0\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\end{array} \\,\\mathbf j +\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\begin{array}{|cc|}\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-\\sqrt3 & -1 \\\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t-1 & \\sqrt3\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\\end{array} \\,\\mathbf k \\ \\right] \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt5} \\left\\langle (0-\\sqrt3), -(0-(-1)), (-3-1) \\right\\rangle \\\\[3pt]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt5} \\left\\langle -\\sqrt3, -1, -4 \\right\\rangle.\n\\end{align}\n\\]\n\nBelow is a diagram of the curve [math]\\mathbf{r}(t),[/math] along with its tangent, normal, and binormal vectors at [math]t=\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}.[/math] Notice that [math]\\mathbf{T}[/math] and [math]\\mathbf{N}[/math] are both orthogonal to [math]\\mathbf{B}.[/math]\n\n![](images/95/95a892eb30b26d1255d29dcaaac552663443c00b2db6fe1e9168a77be061f2c0.png)\n\nSince $\\mathbf B = \\mathbf T\\times \\mathbf N,$ we can conclude that $\\mathbf B$ is perpendicular to both $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N,$ and it's pointing downward.\n\nAlso, since $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ are perpendicular *unit* vectors, it follows that $\\mathbf B$ is also a unit vector." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186168115 #edb/ref 1065 5544 #edb/ref 17592186