\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}⟨-15,25,-20⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362368 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186362011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362368 #edb/ref 1069 "q-99420" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362368 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362368 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=1,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩, \\\\ N(1) & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}⟨-4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362368 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be578a50-bace-5ae6-a42e-46e5c22a651d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362368 #edb/ref 1074 "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(1) & =T(1)\\times N(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}⟨-4,5,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}⟨(-4-5),-(-4-(-4)),(10-(-8))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}⟨-9,0,18⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371714 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371715 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371714 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127626" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371714 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186371714 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=2$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,1,2⟩, \\\\ N(2) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,2,-1⟩.\\end{